---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi3_70",
  "series": "Band VI 3 (1672-1676); durchgesehener Nachdruck 1980",
  "seq": 70,
  "text": "[[504.10]] <b>70. De elementis cogitandi </b> <span>504.10;0:63:070:76       :L:l^</span>.\n[[504.19]] ^nProbares:ö Si verum est dari aliquam demonstrationem perfectam, quae scilicet\n[[504.20]] nihil sine probatione relinquat, necesse est dari Elementa cogitandi; tum enim primum\n[[504.21]] perfecta erit demonstratio, cum resoluta erunt Omnia. Sed jam video id esse\n[[504.22]] falsum. Et tum primum esse demonstrationem perfectam, cum ad identica perventum\n[[504.23]] est, quod fieri potest, licet omnibus non resolutis; nam et non simplicissima, v. g.\n[[504.24]] parabola, ternarius, de se invicem possunt enuntiari. Contra illud certum est, si Elementa\n[[504.25]] sint cogitandi, certam esse scientiam; seu omnia posse demonstrari. Et contra\n[[504.26]] si omnia possunt demonstrari, videntur aliqua esse cogitandi Elementa.\n[[505.1]] Omnia sophismata veterum pariter et recentiorum veniunt a detorta loquendi\n[[505.2]] ratione. Nimirum, si quis loqui velit, is explicare debet ante omnia, quid vocabulo\n[[505.3]] intelligat, et hanc observare legem, ut ne substituta definitione in locum definiti\n[[505.4]] pugnantia oriantur; sed contra efficere, ut substituta definitione in locum definiti\n[[505.5]] manifesta sive necessaria oriantur. Manifestum seu necessarium primum est, unumquodque\n[[505.6]] esse id quod est, sive non esse id quod non est. Non dico in re quiddam tale\n[[505.7]] esse, sed dico: hanc propositionem a nobis appellari necessariam A est A, et A non est\n[[505.8]] non A, et si A sit BC et (C) sit DE, A fore BDE, has loquendi regulas ubi homines\n[[505.9]] constituere; quicquid his consentaneum est, id vere dictum ponunt.\n[[505.10]] Propositionem voco: A est B, vel A non est B. A vocamus subjectum, B praedicatum,\n[[505.11]] est copulam. Per A autem et B quodlibet nomen nominativi casus intelligi\n[[505.12]] potest. Est B simul, repraesentari potest verbo, ut, est sentiens, id est sentit. Pro est\n[[505.13]] aliquando dici potest fuit, erit: sed his missis redeamus ad simplex A est B, vel si A\n[[505.14]] est B, tunc et C est D.\n[[505.15]] Propositio A est (non est) B. C est (non est) D. Si A est (non est) B, tunc C est\n[[505.16]] ( ( non est ) ) D.\n[[505.17]] Ratiocinari est facere propositionem ex aliis datis, substituendo pro aliquo\n[[505.18]] termino in una datarum, eius praedicatum ex alia.\n[[505.19]] Convincere est ex concessis ratiocinari.\n[[505.20]] Demonstrare est ratiocinari ex concedendis,\n[[505.21]] Concedendae propositiones sunt, quas homines qui colloquntur concedere\n[[505.22]] convenere, ut scilicet secum, cumque aliis possent utiliter loqui. Quam in rem necesse\n[[505.23]] erat, ut is qui loqueretur, signa seu quibus utitur, per alia jam notae significationis\n[[505.24]] explicaret, deinde ut recepta semel definitione constanter uti profiteretur proxime ut\n[[506.1]] permissurum se diceret, ut significatio in locum definiti et generaliter praedicatum in\n[[506.2]] locum subjecti substitueretur; vicissim auditorem his assentiri necesse erat, si modo\n[[506.3]] colloqui vellet. Sunt ergo propositiones concedendae, et ex ipsa sermonis necessitate.\n[[506.4]] Definitio: A est BC, declarante loquente se semper permissurum, ut BC pro A\n[[506.5]] substituatur.\n[[506.6]] Propositio identica absoluta: A est A, A non est non A.\n[[506.7]] Propositio identica Hypothetica: si A est B, et B est C, tunc et A est C.\n[[506.8]] Operae pretium erit, ista rursus considera(re). Homines secum aliisque (nunc)\n[[506.9]] tacite nunc voce nunc scriptis, nunc etiam si vis nutibus aliisque signis colloquuntur.\n[[506.10]] Signa quorum significatio sine declaratione non apparet, declaranda sunt. Declaratio\n[[506.11]] fit vel aliis signis jam cognitis, vel rebus ipsis quae significandae sunt, aut earum\n[[506.12]] exemplis ostensis. Et is qui declarat signum, se eo aliquandiu hoc sensu usurum\n[[506.13]] profitetur, quem explicuit. Declaratio autem illa verbis facta est definitio. Usus\n[[506.14]] verborum porro non in eo tantum consistit, ut significent, sed et ut alicuius gratia\n[[506.15]] significent. Cumque nos aliosque verba usu recepta experiamur certo modo conjungere,\n[[506.16]] unumque alteri substituere; quod Propositionem vocamus; nihil enim aliud est\n[[506.17]] dicere A est B, quam ego permittam ut B substituatur in locum A; ideo efficere\n[[506.18]] conamur, ut alii, imo et imposterum nos ipsi (quos eo modo velut nos ipsos consideramus)\n[[506.19]] eodem semper modo verba conjungamus: ita enim fiet ut in posterum\n[[506.20]] cogitandi colloquendique labor minuatur, possumusque varia ac diversa inter se statim\n[[506.21]] connectere. Hoc autem efficere est probare. Probare itaque propositionem\n[[506.22]] est efficere ut aliquis ea constanter utatur, id est ut praedicatum in subjecti locum\n[[506.23]] substituat. Hoc autem duobus fit modis, vel ratiocinatione, vel ostensione. Ratiocinari\n[[506.24]] est propositionem unam facere ex aliis, substituendo scilicet in locum alicuius\n[[506.25]] termini, in aliqua propositione positi, id quod in alia propositione eius praedicatum.\n[[507.1]] Quodsi propositiones quae assumuntur sunt concessae, ratiocinatio est convictio,\n[[507.2]] si vero sint concedendae, ratiocinatio est demonstratio. Concedendae\n[[507.3]] Propositiones sunt, eae quibus non concessis frustra instituitur sermo. Nempe A est\n[[507.4]] A, et A non est non A. Deinde si A est B, A non erit non B. Nam si ista non\n[[507.5]] admitterentur, nihil certi loqueremur, et pari jure posset quidlibet dici. Hoc amplius.\n[[507.6]] Si A est B et B est C, etiam A est C, nam hoc ipsum volumus, cum facimus propositiones,\n[[507.7]] scilicet praedicatum in subjecti locum substitui posse. Denique A est BC, et\n[[507.8]] BC est A posito BC esse definitionem ipsius A. Denique quoties mihi loquor, concedenda\n[[507.9]] apud me propositio est: Ego sum conscius huius illiusve, quod scilicet sentio.\n[[507.10]] Quicquid ergo hoc modo demonstratum erit, illud verum dicemus.\n",
  "number": "70.",
  "title": "De elementis cogitandi",
  "date": ""
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:70. De elementis cogitandi 504.10;0:63:070:76 :L:l^. ^nProbares:ö Si verum est dari aliquam demonstrationem perfectam, quae scilicet nihil sine probatione relinquat, necesse est dari Elementa cogitandi; tum enim primum perfecta erit demonstratio, cum resoluta erunt Omnia. Sed jam video id esse falsu...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>